# ctxwinnow overhead — fixed per-call context report

ctxwinnow test · sessions whose first timestamp is in [open, open) · min turns 3

- **Sessions:** 10 scanned · 10 eligible main · 0 eligible subagent · 10 main decomposed.
- **Excluded:** 0 too few turns · 0 no usage · 0 filtered · 0 fork (inherits parent context) · 0 continuation.
- **Not decomposed** (eligible main): 0 no tool snapshot (0 pre-2.1.259, 0 other) · 0 sanity guard.
- **Input:** 0 files skipped · 0 malformed lines · 0 sessions compacted before the first call.
- **Oldest session:** 2026-09-01. Claude Code keeps transcripts `cleanupPeriodDays` days (default 30); deleted sessions cannot be measured.
- **Entrypoints** (eligible main): cli 10.
- **Claude Code versions** (eligible): 2.1.270–2.1.283.
- **Attribution:** tool JSON at 4.5 bytes per token (`toolJSONBytesPerToken`, band 4.0–4.8); the other components share the rest of B by bytes (median remainder rate: 3.00 bytes per token). B is exact; component figures are estimates (≈).

## Before and after

Split at 2026-09-10T00:00:00Z: **before** = eligible main sessions whose first timestamp is earlier, **after** = sessions starting on or after it (a settings change applies to sessions started after it). B deltas are exact tokens; component predictions are estimates (≈).

> **Fewer than 20 sessions on a side** (before 6, after 4): the report still prints; weigh every delta against the noise floor.

| Side | Sessions | First | Last | Claude Code | B p50 | B p90 | Decomposed |
|---|---:|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|
| before | 6 | 2026-09-01 | 2026-09-06 | 2.1.270–2.1.283 (2 versions) | 2,200 | — | 6 |
| after | 4 | 2026-09-10 | 2026-09-13 | 2.1.283 | 1,350 | — | 4 |

B p90 is printed only from 10 sessions.

- **Paired delta (primary):** -850 tokens: median over 2 projects with sessions on both sides of (median B after − median B before); covers 3 of 4 after-sessions.
- **Unpaired delta:** -850 tokens (median B after − median B before). Differences smaller than ±200 are indistinguishable from session mix at this n (95th percentile of |median difference| over 1,000 random splits of the before side into two groups of 3).
- **Saving:** 60.1% of after-side input: |paired delta| × after-side calls / after-side input, the input the after-side sessions would have added at the before-side baseline.

Removed = present in ≥ 50% of before decomposed sessions and ≤ 5% after; appeared = the reverse. Predicted ≈tokens come from bytes: tool JSON at 4.5 bytes per token, other components at that side's median remainder rate.

| Change | Component | Before | After | Median bytes | Predicted ≈tokens |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| removed | tool Artifact | 100.0% | 0.0% | 4,500 | ≈-1.0k |
| appeared | tool Monitor | 0.0% | 100.0% | 450 | ≈+100 |

Everything else: ≈+50 (paired delta − Σ predicted).

**Drift:** tool definitions present on both sides whose median size changed by ≥ 20% (bytes, not tokens); a Claude Code upgrade can move B without any settings change.

| Tool | Before bytes | After bytes | Change |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Read | 450 | 675 | +50.0% |

## Baseline

B is the context of a session's first call (input + cache read + cache creation): exact. Every call re-reads it, so its token-turns share is B × N / Σ context over the session's N calls.

**Pooled share (headline): 100.0%** of all input read by the 10 eligible main sessions is the fixed baseline. Typical session: 100.0% (median of per-session shares, median N = 5; this mostly reflects session length).

| Sessions | n | B p50 | B p90 | Pooled share | Typical session | Median N |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| main | 10 | 2,100 | 2,400 | 100.0% | 100.0% | 5 |
| subagent (fixed overhead + task prompt) | 0 | — | — | — | — | — |

## What the baseline is made of

10 of 10 eligible main sessions decomposed. Tool JSON is converted at 4.5 bytes per token; the rest of B is shared by the other components in proportion to their bytes, so components sum to B. Median ≈tokens is taken where the component is present.

