## Suggested levers

Catalogued levers whose user-scope saving reaches 0.5% of main token-turns (`MinBenefit`), ranked by that saving. Savings are ≈tokens from your own sessions; levers overlap, so they are never added up. Snippets use User, Local, Env or Flag scope only — never a committed project settings file, which would change the setting for every collaborator.

### 1. disable-artifact: tool Artifact

- **Status:** VERIFIED 2.1.283 (gate 0): n=1 per mechanism; Local enableArtifact −13,382; env −11,740; flag −12,864; Local deny −12,866; ≈54.3k bytes removed
- **Saving, user scope** (every decomposed session carrying it): ≈1.0k tokens per call over 6 sessions (31 calls) · 30.5% of main token-turns.
- **Saving, project scope** (Local snippet, one per project; 3 projects never called it): ≈1.0k tokens per call over 6 sessions (31 calls) · 30.5% of main token-turns.
- **Usage:** called in 0 of 10 sessions, 0 projects, last used —.
- **Observed presence:** Artifact last sent on 2026-09-06 (Claude Code 2.1.283); absent from the 4 most recent sessions with a tool snapshot (3 projects). Presence reflects past launches, not current settings.
- **Snippets:**
  - User (`~/.claude/settings.json`): `"enableArtifact": false` — no other settings file can re-enable it; delete this line to undo.
  - Local (`.claude/settings.local.json`, keep it gitignored): `"enableArtifact": false` — no other settings file can re-enable it; delete this line to undo.
  - Env: `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_ARTIFACT=1 claude`
  - Flag: `claude --disallowedTools Artifact`
- **Trade-off:** Claude can no longer publish pages; off wins everywhere (Local/Project honoured from 2.1.242)
- **Docs:** https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings-reference

### 2. disable-workflows: tool Workflow

- **Status:** UNVERIFIED: documented at https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings-reference
- **Saving, user scope** (every decomposed session carrying it): ≈200 tokens per call over 3 sessions (15 calls) · 3.0% of main token-turns.
- **Saving, project scope** (Local snippet, one per project; 1 project never called it): ≈200 tokens per call over 3 sessions (15 calls) · 3.0% of main token-turns.
- **Usage:** called in 0 of 10 sessions, 0 projects, last used —.
- **Observed presence:** Workflow last sent on 2026-09-12 (Claude Code 2.1.283); absent from the 1 most recent session with a tool snapshot (1 project). Presence reflects past launches, not current settings.
- **Snippets:**
  - User (`~/.claude/settings.json`): `"enableWorkflows": false`
  - Local (`.claude/settings.local.json`, keep it gitignored): `"enableWorkflows": false`
- **Trade-off:** Also removes bundled workflow commands, `/workflow-authoring` and the ultracode keyword
- **Docs:** https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings-reference

## Limitations

- B is exact; every component figure is an estimate (≈) from the two-rate attribution: tool JSON at 4.5 bytes per token (band 4.0–4.8), the rest of B shared by bytes.
- A transcript is not the wire request: the auto-mode template and wire-only reminders are invisible and end up spread over the non-tool components.
- 0 eligible main sessions could not be decomposed (no tool snapshot or sanity guard); they still count for B and token-turns.
- Token-turns are unweighted: cached and uncached input count the same (measured on the author's sessions, not yours: API-weighted pooled share 17.2% vs 17.7%; 99.4% of later calls read ≥ 0.9·B from cache).
- MCP servers still connecting at the first call add their deferred tool names after B (≈0.4k tokens p50, measured on the author's sessions).
- Subagent baselines are measured but not decomposed.
- Only transcripts Claude Code still keeps are measured (`cleanupPeriodDays`, default 30 days).
- Observed tool presence reflects past launches, not current settings; levers marked UNVERIFIED are documented but not measured on the wire.
